    "['set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ospf 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The \"passive\" concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network without specifying an interface\\n3. The network command uses wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n4. Huawei doesn\\'t have the exact \"passive interface\" concept like Juniper, but advertising the loopback network achieves the same effect of not sending OSPF hellos on that interface', 'trans_template': 'ospf 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The \"passive\" concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network without specifying an interface\\n3. The network command uses wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n4. Huawei doesn\\'t have the exact \"passive interface\" concept like Juniper, but advertising the loopback network achieves the same effect of not sending OSPF hellos on that interface', 'trans_template': 'area 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The \"passive\" concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network without specifying an interface\\n3. The network command uses wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n4. Huawei doesn\\'t have the exact \"passive interface\" concept like Juniper, but advertising the loopback network achieves the same effect of not sending OSPF hellos on that interface', 'trans_template': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0'}]]": 1,
