    "['set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ospf 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The passive interface concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network with a 32-bit mask (0.0.0.0)\\n3. The loopback interface itself doesn't need to be explicitly declared as passive in the interface configuration\", 'trans_template': 'ospf 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The passive interface concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network with a 32-bit mask (0.0.0.0)\\n3. The loopback interface itself doesn't need to be explicitly declared as passive in the interface configuration\", 'trans_template': 'area 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices:\\n1. OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case)\\n2. The passive interface concept is implemented by advertising the loopback network with a 32-bit mask (0.0.0.0)\\n3. The loopback interface itself doesn't need to be explicitly declared as passive in the interface configuration\", 'trans_template': 'network 3.3.3.3 0.0.0.0'}]]": 1,
    "['family inet [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv4-family labeled-unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nipv4-family labeled-unicast\\n##\\n\\nFor Huawei devices, the BGP address family configuration is done within the BGP process context. The equivalent commands would be entered after entering the BGP configuration mode for the respective peer groups (iBGP and eBGP in this case). \\n\\nNote that in Huawei:\\n1. The address family is activated with `ipv4-family labeled-unicast` (no need to specify \"inet\" as in Juniper)\\n2. This would be configured under each respective peer group (iBGP and eBGP) after entering their configuration context', 'trans_template': 'ipv4-family labeled-unicast'}]]": 1,
